course: dictionary
lesson: 2532
title: Deed: what people do
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A deed is something a person actually does, usually on purpose. Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «A good deed» is a kind act, so deed means an act that someone chooses to do.
explain: Scouts and Guides are often asked to do a good deed every day. Heroes do brave deeds. In both cases the deed is an action, not a word or a thought. The phrase «in word and deed» shows the difference: word is what you say, deed is what you do.
explain: Deed can also mean a legal paper. «The deeds to the house» are official papers that prove who owns it. Check the clues: a house and papers about owning it fit the legal meaning, not the action meaning. To check your choice, put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A deed is something someone does on purpose, especially something very good or very bad.
fact: «A good deed» is a kind act, such as helping an old neighbour.
fact: «Brave deeds» are acts of courage, the kind heroes do.
fact: In law, «the deeds to the house» are papers that prove who owns the house or land.
fact: «Deeds not words» means that what you actually do matters more than what you say.
exercise: «She did a good deed when she carried the shopping for her old neighbour.» What is a deed in this sentence? | A loud noise made by a door | *Something someone does on purpose | A type of shopping bag | A legal paper about a house
exercise: «The deeds to the house were kept in a safe.» What are the deeds? | *Legal papers that prove who owns the house | Keys for the front door | Good things people do for others | Tools for building the house
exercise: «Heroes often do brave deeds.» Find and copy the phrase that means acts of courage. | do | often | *brave deeds | heroes
test: «The suffragettes' motto was Deeds not words.» What does this motto mean? | Deeds are a kind of food | Nobody should ever write anything down | *Actions matter more than just talking | Words are more important than actions
test: «Sin means turning away from God and doing wrong in thought, word or deed.» Which of these is a deed? | Thinking about a holiday | Feeling a little bit tired | *Taking something that is not yours | Saying a kind word
exam: Which sentence uses deed to mean a legal paper? | *She signed the deeds to the farm, which proved she owned it | He did a deed of kindness and everyone cheered | The deed of the story was told in a poem | Her deed in the race was very fast
